# Chart colour

Colour can identify a source or represent a quantity. Choose the meaning first. In the maintained household charts, a categorical colour identifies a source or device: it must not change because another source was added, a series was hidden or the brand palette changed. **Vivid and Muted follow the theme's existing colour toggle.** Light and Dark remain separate display modes.

The [machine-readable contract](../reference/chart-colours.json) and repository module `design-system/chart-colours.mjs` are the shared authority for the theme, native Energy adapter and [working examples](../components/chart-examples.html). Do not define another palette inside a chart or demonstration.


## Apply data guidance

The [data guidance](brand-data.html) sets the rules for communicating a result, comparison or uncertainty. The deterministic series colours on this page and the [maintained Energy chart specification](../components/charts.html) remain the operational contract. The quantitative scales below are worked documentation references for newly authored graphics. They do not change native Home Assistant charts or maps.


